# SFT execution status v0.90

2026-09-14. The lint-only recovery and its directly consequent versioned bindings
are complete. The exact proposed source/control checkout passes the unchanged
CI lint policy and 626 pure tests on each of two Python versions. Publication
and native execution still need fresh approval; no commit, push or CI run occurred.
Gate 5 remains incomplete. This is completion of the local correction item from
v0.89, not another roadmap gate.

## What was fixed

Exact Ruff 0.15.1 found five issues in the unpublished frozen closure: unused re,
two host-module import-order issues, one test import-order issue, and a zip call
without explicit strict. The corrected successors remove the unused import,
sort the imports, and set strict=False to preserve the previous zip default.
All original versions and the historical lint baseline remain byte-for-byte intact.
No suppression, baseline expansion, parser/floor/resource-policy change or
training-permission relaxation was introduced.

The dependency changes propagate through the host mount/rootfs/bootstrap,
composition, layout, launch and pipeline modules, the harness/supervisor,
source admission, CI acquisition/verifier and their tests. The worker entry
and both worker manifests are unchanged. Twelve source successors match their
predecessor ASTs after only the declared version/pin/import-order/default
normalizations; this is a regression check, not a formal runtime-equivalence proof.

## Actual local verification

- Exact source checkout: parent 781d4c9de9d6acf9f2161855a6089914b980a294,
  plus exactly 60 prospective source/control/test/workflow files, 1,002,980 bytes.
  It contains all parent tracked Python files, but no data/model payloads or
  local evidence, reports, apps or docs. No unrelated untracked files were copied.
- The unchanged frozen-lint checker examined 1,634 Python files. New findings:
  zero. The existing 815 findings in 163 historical files remain unchanged.
  This is not a claim that every source file is lint-clean.
- 626 tests pass on Python 3.11.15 and 3.13.7 with no errors, failures or skips:
  525 component regressions, 69 CI/acquisition/verifier/workflow regressions,
  28 host-control regressions, and four new parity/default-behavior checks.
  Final processes denied network, process starts, native-library loading and
  ML imports through audit hooks; no denied operation was attempted or ML root loaded.
- PyYAML 6.0.3 parses the actual workflow; its nine phases, 41-minute job cap,
  23-minute native phase and exact-parent/first-attempt guard were checked.
  The source-only verifier authenticates the new 78-file admission.
- All 146 listed preceding source/evidence/policy bindings still match.
  The user repository's tracked and staged diffs remain empty.

Clean-checkout testing caught two leftover dynamic test references and a
Python-version difference in AST dump formatting. These were corrected only
in new test versions before the final passing runs. They were local development
iterations, not retries of a native attempt.

Ruff and PyYAML were acquired from official PyPI in an isolated temporary tool
directory. Their two retained wheels total 10,324,095 bytes. Full network
transport accounting was not measured. There was no GitHub/AWS request, accepted
runtime-archive download, model/tokenizer/dataset access, GPU, inference or SFT.
Project dependencies and global Python packages were not changed.

## Ready next action, after fresh approval

The exact proposed publication is 61 additions: 60 bound source/control/test/
workflow files plus the immutable execution plan. It includes 30 newly authored
files and 30 previously verified unpublished files before the plan. Historical
versions, old evidence and unrelated workspace files are excluded. Do not use
a broad git add.

The v1 draft remains disabled. The new reviewed v2 proposal has the ordinary
private-repository, exact-parent, first-attempt guard. It is not published and
does not confer execution authority merely by existing locally.

Approve and bind configs/lumi-4b-sft-prepared-qualification-execution-plan-v0.1.json
before any publication or native action. The proposal allows one non-force
successor push, one fresh GitHub-hosted Ubuntu CPU qualification, accepted
software acquisition, exact owned cleanup and bounded aggregate retrieval.
It includes the automatic Source/Spark jobs: at most 96 configured aggregate
runner-minutes (41 + 35 + 20), not a cost or elapsed-time prediction.

Before push, bounded live checks must confirm the private repository, unchanged
parent, no open PR and no active CI that would be cancelled. Missing/expired
software, moved parent, binding drift or a started failure stops without a native
retry, substitute artifact, image rebuild or permission bypass.

The native part uses one generator guard followed by one prepared-import guard,
two software roots, a 1,200-second harness including its 120-second cleanup
reserve, and at most 120 additional supervisor seconds. It needs at least
16 GiB free disk. No GPU or H100 is needed. Only four closed aggregate receipts
may be retained. Source/Spark's ordinary synthetic tests and dependency traffic
are explicitly distinguished from the new native job's zero forward/optimizer
and no-real-input limits; their full test-internal counters are not measured here.

## What this does not complete

Full Source/Spark CI and the new native Linux path have not run remotely.
A passing tiny qualification still leaves dedicated-host/runtime and
external-writer admission, full-size resource admission, separately authorized
real-checkpoint CPU import, GPU-worker/private-data/CUDA-smoke prerequisites,
and SFT/evaluation. No remaining gate or permission has been marked complete.

Local result:
evidence/lumi-4b-sft-prepared-qualification-lint-recovery-v0.1.json
